---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { absoluteUrl, seo } from '../data/seo';

const meta = seo.home;
const siteUrl = Astro.site?.toString() || 'https://tensor-website.pages.dev/';
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebSite',
  name: 'TENSOR',
  url: absoluteUrl(siteUrl, '/'),
  description: meta.description,
};
---

<BaseLayout title={meta.title} description={meta.description} canonicalPath={meta.canonicalPath} ogType={meta.ogType} hidePageTitle={true} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <section class="section-hero">
    <div class="hero-glow hero-glow-a" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="hero-glow hero-glow-b" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="hero-content container">
      <div class="hero-logo">
        <img src="/assets/img/logo-tensor-framework.png" alt="TENSOR Framework" />
      </div>
      <div class="hero-text">
        <p class="hero-kicker">A public standard for cyber investigations</p>
        <h1 class="hero-title">One investigation.<br />Shared understanding.</h1>
        <p class="hero-definition">Questions, evidence, and decisions that humans and agents can carry between tools.</p>
        <p class="hero-tagline">TENSOR defines a common investigative layer. Public profiles, vendor tools, and business policies build on it while keeping uncertainty, attribution, and history intact.</p>
        <div class="cta-group">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/investigation-lab/" data-telemetry-event="cta-open-investigation-lab" data-telemetry-location="home-hero">Try an investigation</a>
          <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/core/" data-telemetry-event="cta-open-core" data-telemetry-location="home-hero">Read the Core contract</a>
        </div>
        <p class="candidate-status"><span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> Review preview · Core 0.1.0-draft.1 implementation candidate</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container investigation-example" aria-labelledby="example-title">
    <div class="example-intro">
      <p class="section-kicker">See what travels with the case</p>
      <h2 id="example-title">Did the agent send restricted information?</h2>
      <p>A recorded tool call starts the investigation. It does not answer every question. Keep the original assessment, the new evidence, and the resulting decision together.</p>
      <a href="/investigation-lab/">Inspect the synthetic AI-system case →</a>
    </div>
    <ol class="example-trace">
      <li><span class="trace-type">Question instance</span><p>A specific agent, outbound call, time window, and policy context.</p></li>
      <li><span class="trace-type">Initial assessment · unknown</span><p>The call is visible; the transmitted content is not yet established.</p></li>
      <li><span class="trace-type">New evidence and revision</span><p>A receipt changes the assessment. The earlier entry and its inputs remain.</p></li>
      <li><span class="trace-type">Explicit decision</span><p>Record the selected assessment, rationale, policy, and claimed authority. A decision is distinct from execution.</p></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="section-features container" aria-label="What Core preserves">
    <article class="feature-card">
      <h2>Questions with context</h2>
      <p>Separate a reusable definition from a question about a particular subject and time. Pin the meaning used in each investigation.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="feature-card">
      <h2>Unknowns and disagreement</h2>
      <p>Distinguish missing evidence from a negative finding. Preserve competing assessments and make selected decisions explicit.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="feature-card">
      <h2>A history you can hand off</h2>
      <p>Keep evidence references, attribution, original inputs, and revisions together. Declare omissions and unsupported meaning during exchange.</p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="container prose-card" aria-labelledby="layers-title">
    <p class="section-kicker">Public meaning. Room to build.</p>
    <h2 id="layers-title">The shared layer beneath tools and policy</h2>
    <div class="layer-stack" role="img" aria-label="Human and agent investigators use vendor tools and business policy above public TENSOR profiles and Core. Core connects pinned definitions with portable records.">
      <div class="layer-actors">Human investigators <span aria-hidden="true">+</span> Agent investigators</div>
      <div class="layer-pair"><div><strong>Vendor layer</strong><span>Tools, integrations, storage, execution</span></div><div><strong>Business layer</strong><span>Policy, authority, thresholds, retention</span></div></div>
      <div class="layer-public"><strong>Public TENSOR profiles</strong><span>Domain questions, vocabulary, evidence requirements</span></div>
      <div class="layer-core"><strong>TENSOR Core</strong><span>Shared investigative meaning · Pinned definitions + portable records</span></div>
    </div>
    <p>No vendor or business layer may silently change the meaning of Core. Actor type grants no authority. Imported records do not authorize actions or access to evidence.</p>
    <p><a href="/about/">Read the mission and boundaries</a> · <a href="/extensions/">Build profiles and extensions</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="container path-grid">
    <article class="prose-card">
      <p class="section-kicker">For practitioners</p>
      <h2>Start with a real investigative need</h2>
      <p>Explore an AI-system incident or a conventional identity case. Both are synthetic, and both use the same candidate contract for human and agent participation.</p>
      <p>AI security teams are the first adoption community. TENSOR's scope remains all cyber investigations.</p>
      <a href="/investigation-lab/">Open Investigation Lab →</a>
    </article>
    <article class="prose-card">
      <p class="section-kicker">For implementers</p>
      <h2>Validate, exchange, report the gaps</h2>
      <p>Use versioned schemas, a documented binding, and a reference CLI. Build a reader or exporter and test which meaning survives the handoff.</p>
      <p>Reference checks establish a bounded baseline. Independent exchange and external review are the next evidence gates.</p>
      <a href="/implement/">Follow the implementation guide →</a>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="container prose-card">
    <p class="section-kicker">Built from the existing foundation</p>
    <h2>The investigation questions stay</h2>
    <p>The legacy release contains 588 questions and 1,554 transitions. Its original artifacts remain available while the questions undergo semantic review for the new definition-and-record model.</p>
    <p><a href="/questions/">Browse the question catalog</a> · <a href="/graphs/">View preserved releases</a> · <a href="/studio/">Open legacy Graph Studio</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="container prose-card">
    <p class="section-kicker">Help shape a public standard</p>
    <h2>Useful alongside the standards you already use</h2>
    <p>TENSOR's proposed boundaries reference ATT&amp;CK, D3FEND, ATLAS, CASE/UCO, STIX, Attack Flow, CACAO, and OCSF. Mappings need versioned definitions and exchange evidence; they are not implied by a logo or a shared field name.</p>
    <p>The founding charter, governance proposal, and 38 Core requirements are open for review. This candidate is not a ratified standard or an institutional endorsement.</p>
    <div class="cta-group"><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/standards/">Explore the standards crosswalk</a><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/contribute/">Contribute a case or review</a></div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .candidate-status { margin-top: 1.15rem; font-size: 0.83rem; color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .status-dot { display: inline-block; width: 0.45rem; height: 0.45rem; margin-right: 0.4rem; background: var(--accent-primary); border-radius: 50%; vertical-align: middle; }
  .investigation-example { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 0.95fr 1.05fr; gap: 3rem; padding: 2rem 2.2rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--line-soft); border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-primary); }
  .example-intro h2 { font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 2.6vw, 2rem); line-height: 1.3; margin: 0.7rem 0 1rem; }
  .example-intro p { color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .example-trace { list-style: none; padding: 0; counter-reset: trace; }
  .example-trace li { position: relative; padding: 0 0 1.2rem 2.4rem; border-left: 1px solid var(--line-soft); }
  .example-trace li:last-child { padding-bottom: 0; border-left-color: transparent; }
  .example-trace li::before { counter-increment: trace; content: counter(trace); position: absolute; left: -0.8rem; top: 0; width: 1.6rem; height: 1.6rem; border: 1px solid var(--line-soft); border-radius: 50%; background: var(--bg-card); font: 0.75rem/1.5rem var(--font-mono); text-align: center; color: var(--accent-primary); }
  .trace-type { font: 600 0.8rem/1.4 var(--font-mono); color: var(--accent-primary); }
  .example-trace p { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.93rem; margin-top: 0.2rem; }
  .feature-card h2 { font-size: 1.2rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .layer-stack { margin: 1.5rem 0; display: grid; gap: 0.7rem; }
  .layer-actors { text-align: center; padding: 0.4rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .layer-actors > span { color: var(--accent-primary); padding: 0 1rem; }
  .layer-pair { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 0.7rem; }
  .layer-pair > div, .layer-public, .layer-core { padding: 1rem 1.3rem; border: 1px solid var(--line-soft); background: var(--bg-input); }
  .layer-stack strong, .layer-stack span { display: block; }
  .layer-actors > span { display: inline; }
  .layer-stack span { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .layer-core { border-color: var(--accent-primary); border-left-width: 3px; }
  .layer-core strong { color: var(--accent-primary); }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .investigation-example { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.6rem; padding: 1.5rem; }
    .example-trace { margin-left: 0.8rem; }
    .layer-pair { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .layer-actors { font-size: 0.9rem; }
    .layer-actors > span { padding: 0 0.4rem; }
  }
</style>
